# C2-S10, the Clock Tower, B02 The Minute Hand, C2-S11 The Missing Shift.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2345–2407.
# "bell" plays in the region when the player approaches the tower; the rest in
# scenes/chapter2/clock_tower.tscn.

# C2-S10 — the bell rings thirteen times, then stops.
~ bell
do bell_thirteen
Kaelen (Internal): ...eleven. Twelve. Thirteen.
# Then silence. Merchants stop. Children count on their fingers. Paladins look up.
Brask: Lower streets. Every gate, every stair. Sealed, now.
Seraphina: Brask, half the lower city's still out on those stairs. We don't know what this is yet.
Brask: That is why we seal them.
do data_vision_trace
System: TRACE: CLOCK AUTHORITY CONFLICT.
System: TRACE: LEGACY SCHEDULES ACTIVE.
System: TRACE: EXTERNAL ADMIN PROXY.
Kaelen: Two schedules fighting over one bell. And something outside the tower's got its hand on the rope.
Seraphina: Then we climb up and ask it nicely. Once.
[if ch2_medicine_quest_active and not ch2_medicine_done] Seraphina: And the convoy's still out. Forty-two people, and the west gate's closing on them. That was the evening bell, Kaelen.
set ch2_tower_bell_stopped

~ entry
Kaelen: Every gear on this floor's keeping its own time. That one's fast. That one's a whole tick behind—
Elara: They're arguing. Like Wenna and Tull over the sluice.
Kaelen: Yes— that's it. Two rules on one axle, and nobody's told either of them it lost.
Kaelen (Internal): Root Access could slow one of these down. Only a little, if I want to do it safely, and never all the way to a stop.

# A mark scratched into the wall on the way up (a seed for Kaito, later).
~ mid
Kaelen (Internal): Someone's scratched a little map mark into the stone here. Under it, cut deeper: NO SKY ABOVE FLOOR SIX.
Elara: Is there sky above floor six? Somebody wanted it said badly enough to use a knife.
Kaelen: I'm not checking. If somebody carved a warning into a staircase, I'm taking the staircase's word for it.
set ch2_tower_secret_mark

~ pre_boss
System: SCHEDULE DEVIATION.
Kaelen: That's us. We're the deviation.
Seraphina: I've hated clocks before. Departure boards. The galley timer. The one over the cockpit door.
Seraphina: None of them ever told me I was the mistake.

# ── B02 The Minute Hand: barks, one line each ─────────────────────────────
~ bark_deviation
The Minute Hand: SCHEDULE DEVIATION.

~ bark_correct
The Minute Hand: CORRECT.

~ bark_replay
The Minute Hand: REPLAYING.

~ victory
Kaelen: That's half the tower back on one clock. The top half's still taking orders from somewhere else.
System: SHIFT LOG: LOWER WORKS, SHIFT FOUR — ENTERED 06:00. EXIT: NONE.
set ch2_clock_tower_complete
=> missing_shift

# C2-S11 — the missing shift. Not the faction choice; every option costs something.
~ missing_shift
Seraphina: Shift four. Forty workers went down at six this morning, and I've had the gate count read to me twice. Nobody's come up.
Brask: Lower works. Quarantined, from now until we know what's down there.
Seraphina: We know what's down there. Forty people.
? Kaelen (Internal): Not my city, not my shift. And they're both looking at me like I've got the deciding vote.
- Now. Every hour down there is an hour they might not have. => rescue_now
- Scout first. I want to know what's down there before it knows we're coming. => scout_first
- Seal it until morning. Nobody else goes down there and doesn't come back tonight. => seal

~ rescue_now
set ch2_shift_rescue_now
do trust seraphina 10
Seraphina: Then get your things, please. Market stairs. I'll count us in at the top.
Brask: If you lose a single paladin down there, Commander—
Seraphina: Then you'll write it down, and I'll read it.
=> unlock

~ scout_first
set ch2_shift_scout_first
Seraphina: That'll cost us hours, and forty people are paying for every one of them.
Kaelen: If we walk in blind, you'll be counting us too.
Seraphina: ...Hours, then. Not one minute past them. I'll be counting those as well.
=> unlock

~ seal
set ch2_shift_sealed
do trust seraphina -10
Brask: Thank you. Lower works, sealed until dawn. I'll write it exactly that way.
Seraphina: Don't thank him. Forty people, and he's just bought whatever's down there a whole night to get worse.
=> unlock

~ unlock
set ch2_underground_unlocked
